{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1505792-chronicle-project","id":1505792,"title":"Chronicle Project","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-03-19T10:33:14-07:00","id":1505792,"title":"Chronicle Project","content":"This is an idea I had for a chronicle and I wanted a second opinion if possible.<br /> <br /> &quot;In the city of Portland (Temporary) recently there have been extremely violent attacks involving women, suspecting that this could be Formori attacks due to their nature a pack of Black Furies come to the city to deal with the situation, however, the territory belongs to a pack of Glass Walkers belonging the Dies Ultima and due to problems that the two tribes had already had in their past they did not gave permission for the pack to enter, however one of the Garou didn't want to wait and entered the city alone and unnoticed, in order to avoid a quarrel the Furies ask for help from a another pack nearby (The players' pack) so that they can enter the city and take out the Fury without the Glass Walkers noticing that she has invaded.\u200b&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-19T14:57:05-07:00","id":1505827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1505792-chronicle-project#post1505792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;In the city of Portland (Temporary) recently there have been extremely violent attacks involving women, suspecting that this could be Formori attacks due to their nature a pack of Black Furies come to the city to deal with the situation,</div> </div> </div> </div>From where? Why? How did they learn about this? Why don't they have pressing concerns in their Sept?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1505792-chronicle-project#post1505792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">however, the territory belongs to a pack of Glass Walkers belonging the Dies Ultima</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a really, really weird choice. Dies Ultimae are not really a big camp, and I doubt they have much to do in a city. To all outwards appearances they are a large mercenary group that operates in high risk territories and warzones. In actuality they are a combination military unit, combination doomsday cult which believes in all out warfare against the Wyrm using modern weapons and tactics and using their kinfolk (Homid and Lupus) as support units for their actions. I suggest you go for another group of Glass Walkers instead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1505792-chronicle-project#post1505792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b and due to problems that the two tribes had already had in their past they did not gave permission for the pack to enter,</div> </div> </div> </div>What problem? When? Who is perpetuating this conflict? How do you define this territory? This isn't Forsaken where whole cities could be claimed as territory of the Werewolves, in Apocalypse usually the territory the local Sept controls is the Caern, it's Bawn and maybe a site or two of spiritual or kinfolk significance. That would not cover a city the size of a Portland. And if horrifying murders are happening in their neighbourhood, why aren't the Glass Walkers doing something about it? It's not like it's beneficial to them for things like this to go around, heck considering that they are one of the most informed tribes most tapped into day to day happenings, they'd be first to notice something was wrong about this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1505792-chronicle-project#post1505792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bhowever one of the Garou didn't want to wait and entered the city alone and unnoticed, in order to avoid a quarrel the Furies ask for help from a another pack nearby (The players' pack) so that they can enter the city and take out the Fury without the Glass Walkers noticing that she has invaded.\u200b&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Now, who the hell is the player pack in all of this? Where are they from? Why would the Glass Walkers listen to them? Why does the PC pack even care about the gung-ho Fury or her pack?<br /> <br /> <br /> The framework itself is not bad, but it assumes that there will be a nearby homogeneous Black Fury Sept, a homogeneous Glass Walker sept and a (most likley considering it's PC's) mixed sept nearby. Three septs and three Caerns in such a small area doesn't really sound probable. I'd simplify things and just have the pack looking for a missing Black Fury that got in way over her head and trying to prevent a fallout between two septs (one in portland and one a bt further away) as the missing Fury has had a feud with the local Sept leader, and whoever sends the pack is trying to prevent things escalating further.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":1182,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","user":"Asmodai","date":". 03-19-2023, 06:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-19T16:26:39-07:00","id":1505836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1505792-chronicle-project?p=1505827#post1505827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From where? Why? How did they learn about this? Why don't they have pressing concerns in their Sept?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This pack of Furies is not big, 5 garou, plus half a dozen Kinfolks, they are one of those who believe that a way to fight the Wyrm is to end injustices committed with women, in that they ended up forming a network of contacts, one of them being a Kinfolk linked to the Glass Walkers, not the Dies Ultima, she is a hacker who communicates with them via correspondence. (She is one of my cards in the hole). As for urgency, the crime scene has traces of Formori activity, residue to be exact, so they decided to investigate if this wasn't the start of something bigger.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1505792-chronicle-project?p=1505827#post1505827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a really, really weird choice. Dies Ultimae are not really a big camp, and I doubt they have much to do in a city. To all outwards appearances they are a large mercenary group that operates in high risk territories and warzones. In actuality they are a combination military unit, combination doomsday cult which believes in all out warfare against the Wyrm using modern weapons and tactics and using their kinfolk (Homid and Lupus) as support units for their actions. I suggest you go for another group of Glass Walkers instead.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>As for the presence of the Dies Ultima, they have established a base in the city for future operations, something they are preparing in the future in combination with other groups of Garou, this is indeed what it sounds like, an excuse to use the Dies Ultima, but also I can use this as a hook for future quests, but if it's too much trouble, I'll switch to, I don't know their name in English, but they're the mafia wolves.<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1505792-chronicle-project?p=1505827#post1505827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What problem? When? Who is perpetuating this conflict? How do you define this territory? This isn't Forsaken where whole cities could be claimed as territory of the Werewolves, in Apocalypse usually the territory the local Sept controls is the Caern, it's Bawn and maybe a site or two of spiritual or kinfolk significance. That would not cover a city the size of a Portland. And if horrifying murders are happening in their neighbourhood, why aren't the Glass Walkers doing something about it? It's not like it's beneficial to them for things like this to go around, heck considering that they are one of the most informed tribes most tapped into day to day happenings, they'd be first to notice something was wrong about this.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that between 2 and 3 years ago 3 Black Furies appeared in the city asking for refuge, they accepted, but had a attack during their stay and there was a massacre on both sides and the two groups accused each other, this caused a complication between Dies Ultima and the Furies and it almost didn't become a bigger problem. To be clear, the pack that tried to enter the city wasn't even involved with the incident, but the Dies Ultima are paranoid when it comes to Black Furies. As for the Dies Ultima not realizing it, in fact they realized that there is something strange, but for them it seems like a trap so they are dealing with it more calmly, and already telling you what I'm planning, they are not wrong, but that's just half truth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1505792-chronicle-project?p=1505827#post1505827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> Now, who the hell is the player pack in all of this? Where are they from? Why would the Glass Walkers listen to them? Why does the PC pack even care about the gung-ho Fury or her pack?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The question of placing the PCs is that improvised thing, I didn't do it thinking about a specific group that I already know, so I would adapt with what I had, maybe one of them has contact in the city or knows one of the Furies, or even one of the victims was an acquaintance and they ended up getting involved. As for why the Glass Walkers would accept them, I never said they would accept them easily, but a pack from another tribe or multitribal would have a better chance than a pack of Black Furies given the city's past.<br /> <br /> I forgeted something?<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-20T15:08:35-07:00","id":1505944,"title":"","content":"It's your game, so none of it is a problem per se. What you say is what happens, I'm just giving feedback based on the general notes in the setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1505792-chronicle-project?p=1505836#post1505836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This pack of Furies is not big, 5 garou, plus half a dozen Kinfolks, they are one of those who believe that a way to fight the Wyrm is to end injustices committed with women, in that they ended up forming a network of contacts, one of them being a Kinfolk linked to the Glass Walkers, not the Dies Ultima, she is a hacker who communicates with them via correspondence. (She is one of my cards in the hole). As for urgency, the crime scene has traces of Formori activity, residue to be exact, so they decided to investigate if this wasn't the start of something bigger.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>5 Garou is not a small pack. And it's quite uncommon for kinfolk to travel with a pack (it's one of the reasons why the Dies Ultimae are considered weird). However, a bigger concern from a worldbuilding perspective for me is where are they coming from. Packs usually don't randomly roam the land - those that do are looked at with a lot of prejudice and wary eyes. It's especially odd to have one such pack that's monotribal. One would expect that they come from a place where they could have recruited 5 Black Furies AND that could have spared them waltzing around. It seems like a missed opportunity to not have another Sept &quot;nearby&quot; which could build up interplay for the Septs. One could see the Furies protecting a Wyld or Nature Caern, maybe near Mt. Hood?<br /> <br /> Also Portland is a stone's thrown away from Vancouver, with it's very messy and complicated history in the WoD, and especially Werewolf. Are you planning to integrate elements from that?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1505792-chronicle-project?p=1505836#post1505836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> As for the presence of the Dies Ultima, they have established a base in the city for future operations, something they are preparing in the future in combination with other groups of Garou, this is indeed what it sounds like, an excuse to use the Dies Ultima, but also I can use this as a hook for future quests, but if it's too much trouble, I'll switch to, I don't know their name in English, but they're the mafia wolves.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> The Mafia wolves are called Wiseguys. But most Glass Walkers don't belong to a camp. The Camps are just subgroups, and Dies Ultimae are a very extreme one (even if they are presented as growing).<br /> <br /> There are maybe 10 packs of them of combined kinfolk and garou strikeforces that are placed in locations where they can react to the commands of Robert Petkov and the visions of his wife Tsuki. Their main base is a training facility somewhere in west Australia. Now they did start as a mercenary company &quot;with a strict ethical code&quot; that provided special services and employed Garou. They go out and kill, destroy, explode and demolish anything belonging to the Wyrm, sometimes missing the mark. But they never were really big. If you're going with Portland as their territory is this because you see them having a base there? Offices? A proper Caern? I don't really see them keeping many Caerns considering the methodology of their work. Considering that you cannot really have them using their methodology in USA without getting a lot of heat, any Dies Utlimae operating on US soil would be extra careful not to get attention from the government and would most likely be involved in bodyguard work, site security and intelligence gathering. None of that really screams the cool parts of who the Dies Ultimae are.<br /> <br /> The best explanation I can have for it is that they had a small urban Caern that was the original HQ of the PMC that would become the camp, and that they still keep offices above it and have kinfolk doing low key stuff that won't gather attention. There might be a pack protecting it, but how likely is it that these will be the bad ass mercenaries taking the battle to the Wyrm? It's more likely to be general Glass Walkers recruited to help out with the Sept and more subtle or teritorrial Dies Ultimae Garou that didn't see the point in chasing the Wyrm around the world when their Caern here still needs protection.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1505792-chronicle-project?p=1505836#post1505836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> The problem is that between 2 and 3 years ago 3 Black Furies appeared in the city asking for refuge, they accepted, but had a attack during their stay and there was a massacre on both sides and the two groups accused each other, this caused a complication between Dies Ultima and the Furies and it almost didn't become a bigger problem. To be clear, the pack that tried to enter the city wasn't even involved with the incident, but the Dies Ultima are paranoid when it comes to Black Furies. As for the Dies Ultima not realizing it, in fact they realized that there is something strange, but for them it seems like a trap so they are dealing with it more calmly, and already telling you what I'm planning, they are not wrong, but that's just half truth.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>So what caused this problem, and why isn't it a problem this time? Wouldn't it be even better if this third party (vampires, maybe?) is literally itching at any chance to have the Garou destroy themselves now, after all they are giving them this chance on the platter, and in a City walls have ears. Again you've got a bit weird conception about what kind of teritorry a Sept or a pack controls - it's quite possible for a pack to be in a city and never even know that there is an urban Sept of Glass Walkers or Bone Gnawers if they don't actively look for it.<br /> <br /> And Portland is weird choice for a number of reasons - it's a smaller city, it's got a lot of wilderness around it. It's traditionally the territory of the Pure Tribes - One would think the Younger Brother or Older Brother would have a presence here. Maybe among the Chinook? Again, you're faced with the shadow of Vancouver and all the weirdness that happened there including the vampire pacts and the Gaian Prophet. I'd honestly avoid that, but you probably have a reason why you want to be there.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1505792-chronicle-project?p=1505836#post1505836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> The question of placing the PCs is that improvised thing, I didn't do it thinking about a specific group that I already know, so I would adapt with what I had, maybe one of them has contact in the city or knows one of the Furies, or even one of the victims was an acquaintance and they ended up getting involved. As for why the Glass Walkers would accept them, I never said they would accept them easily, but a pack from another tribe or multitribal would have a better chance than a pack of Black Furies given the city's past.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Again. WHERE are they from. Which sept do they belong to? Their credibility is influenced by the elders and the sept they are from as well as opening interesting interplay between them and the City Garou. Garou congregate around Caerns, creating communities called Septs. You need to define the septs and their interests as well as how thee packs you want to use belong somewhere. If they are just a random roving pack there is zero credibility there and no reason for them to be any better than the Furies.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-20T16:40:29-07:00","id":1505968,"title":"","content":"Okay, first of all my mouse is giving me trouble, so I'm sorry for not making this cute, now take a breath and pay attention:<br /> <br /> 1. First the choice of Portland, it was just an illustrative choice I don't intend to use Portland, I just chose the first city that came to my mind at the time, so let's try to ignore that part so we won't have a headache, in fact I don't even know whether I was really going to use a real city, or a fictional one;<br /> <br /> 2. You asked about the Furies, they don't travel randomly, they just have an objective that requires them to make trips, I've already explained which one and they can separate if necessary, there are some determined courses, routes they use and so on.<br /> <br /> 3. As for the size of the pack, this can be a confusion that I made from my habit, but I've seen others ST running and there were packs that could have 20 Garou and yes there are some systems for that to work, but I won't stretching for now, it could be something they invented and I'm not used to it, but anyway, just ignore it for now;<br /> <br /> 4. As for the presence of the Dies Ultima, Ok I'll rephrase that later, how about a pack that is receiving training from one of the Dies Ultima, good now?<br /> <br /> 5. Leaving for the attack of 2 or 3 years ago I was thinking of an attack by the Skindancers, they entered and it turned into that slaughter, bodies missing from both sides raised suspicions and they weren't all there so only part of the packs died, but I nothing is defined yet, as I said it's a project I don't have everything ready yet.<br /> <br /> 6. As for the slaughter being a problem in the current time of the chronicle, that was the situation, neither of the two groups wanted to start a war there even if for revenge, not least because, as I said, there were suspicions, but no proof, so the case ended without more blood was spilled, but there are still members in the pack who were afraid, as a result they were left with trauma and prejudice from the Black Furies in general and bacause this the had that attitude, they didn't let them in because of paranoia.<br /> <br /> 7. As for the players, I already said that this wasn't thought for a specific group, I'll improvise depending on the case so I can't answer you because I don't know myself.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-20T17:31:04-07:00","id":1505973,"title":"","content":"Hey, you don't need my permission to make your own game. You're the one that asked for feedback.<br /> <br /> Again. I feel you're missing out a lot by not working out which Sept is where and how they interact with each other. Just using vagabond packs seems like a waste in a chronicle based on social conflict between two groups ostensibly on the same side. A sept of 20 Garou is pretty damn big, usually reserved for highest rank Caerns and Werewolf LARP's. It's not impossible to make a Pack of 20, but that doesn't really make a lot of sense with the setting as presented. You don't really have that many Garou all changing at the same time and all joined together into a Pack. And considering how intimate the bond of a Pack is, I'm not really sure it'd be benefited by a huge pack - how many people are you willing to share your toothbrush with? <br /> <br /> There is a possibility that for something epic you might make a Wave Sentai, War Pack or Kganmadi that would have 20 members, but such a gathering of shifters is a thing of legends.<br /> <br /> And 7 is probably the biggest problem. You will need a way to integrate all the Player Characters and their ecletic tribe choices into this, the easiest way for this is to build a sept for them with their local mentors, elders and spirits and then build up from their concepts something that integrates them to the setting and the conflict you're building.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-20T18:01:02-07:00","id":1505982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1505792-chronicle-project?p=1505973#post1505973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, you don't need my permission to make your own game. You're the one that asked for feedback.<br /> <br /> Again. I feel you're missing out a lot by not working out which Sept is where and how they interact with each other. Just using vagabond packs seems like a waste in a chronicle based on social conflict between two groups ostensibly on the same side. A sept of 20 Garou is pretty damn big, usually reserved for highest rank Caerns and Werewolf LARP's. It's not impossible to make a Pack of 20, but that doesn't really make a lot of sense with the setting as presented. You don't really have that many Garou all changing at the same time and all joined together into a Pack. And considering how intimate the bond of a Pack is, I'm not really sure it'd be benefited by a huge pack - how many people are you willing to share your toothbrush with?<br /> <br /> There is a possibility that for something epic you might make a Wave Sentai, War Pack or Kganmadi that would have 20 members, but such a gathering of shifters is a thing of legends.<br /> <br /> And 7 is probably the biggest problem. You will need a way to integrate all the Player Characters and their ecletic tribe choices into this, the easiest way for this is to build a sept for them with their local mentors, elders and spirits and then build up from their concepts something that integrates them to the setting and the conflict you're building.</div> </div> </div> </div>First at all, sorry if I looked angry or anything, but today was a juggling of things and the tecnology don't help me, so I lose my temper.<br /> <br /> Second, I've seen people running campaigns around here, and at least in the groups that I've seen that they do things could range from families, small communities, small towns and a lot of those keeping in touch, so they looked more like organizations to be honest, I've seen they put an organized group (NPC) that should have a dozen Bone Gnawers acting together, but out of necessity they barely spent time together, Glass Walkers who are really relatives, they get together when a job needs to be done, but each one has their life and they are the kind of people that if it weren't for blood they wouldn't have to mix. My point in saying this is, I think I have a somewhat warped view of how packs work. So sorry if I make some confusion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-20T19:24:41-07:00","id":1505999,"title":"","content":"I think you're just mixing up a Sept and a Pack from this description.<br /> <br /> A pack is a small group of tightly knit werewolves who usually passed their rite of passage together (not always). It usually consists of 3-6 werewolves. The pack is bound together by a common totem (the totem background) that ties them together and allows them to feel each other and coordinate perfectly in battle. The knock on effect is that people who spend time in a pack are closer than family.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Sept\" target=\"_blank\">A sept </a>is a community of Werewolves and Kinfolk that centres around a Caern. Usually a Sept is controlled by one or two tribes, but there are some that can include more. These include the grounds of the Caern and any important parts of the local area that they can protect (the Bawn). A sept consists of Garou leading it taking certain positions in the structure and a number of packs that belong to the Sept, but are individual units. For smaller sept that could mean 2-3 elders and a single young pack, for the biggest ones it could be a dozen assorted Garou (who are either too young for a pack or who lost their packs and found meaning in Sept duties) and a dozen packs.The sept is in charge of organising the local Garou and making sure that the Wyrm is fought, the Caern is kept safe, spirits are placated and moots are held to revitalize the Caern.<br /> <br /> Usually the sept is colored by the tribes that makeup its leadership and the history of it as a Caern. Most of them are Wilderness areas, but some are in the middle of the City (especially Bone Gnawer and Glass Walker Caerns). Most of them are very old and have had protectors for centuries. Oh and each Caern has a Totem spirit which the Sept is allied with and protects, but they don't leave the Caern as they are an embodiment of the holy place rather than the spirits that follow packs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":1182,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","user":"Asmodai","date":". 03-20-2023, 10:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-21T00:31:52-07:00","id":1506016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1505792-chronicle-project?p=1505999#post1505999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're just mixing up a Sept and a Pack from this description.<br /> <br /> A pack is a small group of tightly knit werewolves who usually passed their rite of passage together (not always). It usually consists of 3-6 werewolves. The pack is bound together by a common totem (the totem background) that ties them together and allows them to feel each other and coordinate perfectly in battle. The knock on effect is that people who spend time in a pack are closer than family.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Sept\" target=\"_blank\">A sept </a>is a community of Werewolves and Kinfolk that centres around a Caern. Usually a Sept is controlled by one or two tribes, but there are some that can include more. These include the grounds of the Caern and any important parts of the local area that they can protect (the Bawn). A sept consists of Garou leading it taking certain positions in the structure and a number of packs that belong to the Sept, but are individual units. For smaller sept that could mean 2-3 elders and a single young pack, for the biggest ones it could be a dozen assorted Garou (who are either too young for a pack or who lost their packs and found meaning in Sept duties) and a dozen packs.The sept is in charge of organising the local Garou and making sure that the Wyrm is fought, the Caern is kept safe, spirits are placated and moots are held to revitalize the Caern.<br /> <br /> Usually the sept is colored by the tribes that makeup its leadership and the history of it as a Caern. Most of them are Wilderness areas, but some are in the middle of the City (especially Bone Gnawer and Glass Walker Caerns). Most of them are very old and have had protectors for centuries. Oh and each Caern has a Totem spirit which the Sept is allied with and protects, but they don't leave the Caern as they are an embodiment of the holy place rather than the spirits that follow packs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess you right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-22T09:47:31-07:00","id":1506146,"title":"","content":"Hi Psicose, so everything that\u2019s been said is absolutely correct, however as <b>Asmodai</b>\u200b has said it\u2019s your campaign.<br /> <br /> Some STs and their groups like a very social game centered around a Sept/Caern while others prefer John Wick meets WOD, neither\u2019s wrong whichever your group has more fun from.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s up to you on whether you stick to canon or modify, even the original writers threw in curveball locations, Vancouvers a great example.<br /> <br /> My advice is create a small degree of background for the location, so if a smaller city like Portland is dominated by Glasswalkers why is that, how many Caerns are present.<br /> <br /> Are there multiple GW camps with the Dies Ultima using it as a base of operations to complete black ops on Pentax in the area (are they using a haulage or shipping company as cover), have they formed a tentative alliance with the Wise Guys.<br /> <br /> Did the Corporate Wolves run the inner city caern and Dies Ultima helped the Wiseguys stage a take over.<br /> <br /> Does Portland have a City Father or Mother Spirit who has an axe to grind with the children of Pegasus and therefore pushes the resident GWs to oppose any Black Fury presence, maybe a historical business deal by a Fury kinfolk that went bad way back when.<br /> <br /> You\u2019ve said there\u2019s a growing evil in the city that\u2019s led the Fury to intrude, has a local rural Pure Ones Sept or Pure One plus allied tribe (look at San Francisco Uktena + Children of Gaia) requested a pack from an allied totem to find the Fury and get the GWs to look at the real problem.<br /> <br /> Those are just some ideas for possible background for the city and it\u2019s resident Garou.<br /> <br /> Hope that helps <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-22T13:02:18-07:00","id":1506167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1505792-chronicle-project?p=1506146#post1506146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi Psicose, so everything that\u2019s been said is absolutely correct, however as <b>Asmodai</b>\u200b has said it\u2019s your campaign.<br /> <br /> Some STs and their groups like a very social game centered around a Sept/Caern while others prefer John Wick meets WOD, neither\u2019s wrong whichever your group has more fun from.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s up to you on whether you stick to canon or modify, even the original writers threw in curveball locations, Vancouvers a great example.<br /> <br /> My advice is create a small degree of background for the location, so if a smaller city like Portland is dominated by Glasswalkers why is that, how many Caerns are present.<br /> <br /> Are there multiple GW camps with the Dies Ultima using it as a base of operations to complete black ops on Pentax in the area (are they using a haulage or shipping company as cover), have they formed a tentative alliance with the Wise Guys.<br /> <br /> Did the Corporate Wolves run the inner city caern and Dies Ultima helped the Wiseguys stage a take over.<br /> <br /> Does Portland have a City Father or Mother Spirit who has an axe to grind with the children of Pegasus and therefore pushes the resident GWs to oppose any Black Fury presence, maybe a historical business deal by a Fury kinfolk that went bad way back when.<br /> <br /> You\u2019ve said there\u2019s a growing evil in the city that\u2019s led the Fury to intrude, has a local rural Pure Ones Sept or Pure One plus allied tribe (look at San Francisco Uktena + Children of Gaia) requested a pack from an allied totem to find the Fury and get the GWs to look at the real problem.<br /> <br /> Those are just some ideas for possible background for the city and it\u2019s resident Garou.<br /> <br /> Hope that helps<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I appreciate the idea, but I already have my own plans for septs within the city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-22T15:55:29-07:00","id":1506185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1505792-chronicle-project?p=1506167#post1506167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I appreciate the idea, but I already have my own plans for septs within the city.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad to hear it, hope it all goes well","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}